<article class="env-lemma" id="0FBJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FBJ">Lemma <span data-tag="0FBJ">42.54.1</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Z' \ar[r] \ar[d]_ g &  X' \ar[d]^ f \\  Z \ar[r] &  X }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a cartesian diagram of schemes locally of finite type over $S$ whose horizontal arrows are closed immersions. If $\mathcal{N}$ is a virtual normal sheaf for $Z$ in $X$, then $\mathcal{N}' = g^*\mathcal{N}$ is a virtual normal sheaf for $Z'$ in $X'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from the surjectivity of the map $g^*\mathcal{C}_{Z/X} \to \mathcal{C}_{Z'/X'}$ proved in Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0473" data-tag="0473">29.32.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>